ACCOUNTS AND APPROVAL
  accountapproval list              accounts awaiting approval.
  accountapproval approve <name>    approve one. Logged to
                                    /log/adm/accountapproval.
  A brand-new account created after this MUD already has an admin
  cannot finish character creation until approved. The very first
  account on a fresh install is never flagged, so the first-admin
  bootstrap cannot deadlock.
  Pending accounts also show on the staff bulletin board, so you do not
  have to remember to run the list command.

PROMOTIONS
  makewiz then setrole is the normal pipeline. Both auto-set a default
  who-title for the new rank and correctly progress through titles, but
  neither will overwrite a genuine custom title set another way.
  setrole admin sets position "arch", never "head arch". The founder's
  "head arch" position and its hardcoded who-list title are untouched
  by the role commands.
  Group membership lives in /secure/cfg/groups.cfg. A member-less group
  line such as (AMBASSADOR) is valid by design; master.c load_access()
  has a second sscanf pass for it. Do not "fix" that by requiring a
  trailing space.

LOGS
  log_file() prepends /log/. Pass paths relative to it.
  /log/adm/setrole, /log/adm/accountapproval, /log/errors/<dir> for
  compile failures, /log/runtime for runtime errors. Object load
  failures appear only in log/errors, which is the usual reason a
  "mysteriously missing" object goes unnoticed.

